        doc:participation_fedor_zan_trial_1999,
        doc:participation_prosecution_trial_1999 ;
    echr:hasProceedingStartDate "1999-02-08"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeCriminal ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "In the trial which took place between 8 February and 1 April 1999, before Mr Justice Potts and a jury, the applicant was represented by senior and junior counsel and solicitors."^^xsd:string,
        "On 1 April 1999, the jury convicted the applicant of counts 1 and 3. The applicant was sentenced to a mandatory term of life imprisonment. The trial judge recommended that the applicant “never see the light of day”. The Lord Chief Justice recommended a tariff (the period to be served for retribution and deterrence) of five years. The Home Secretary has yet to fix the tariff."^^xsd:string .

